  <h2 id="federal">The Federal Privacy Law Outlook</h2>
  <p>The American Data Privacy and Protection Act (ADPPA) has been proposed in Congress multiple times but has yet to pass. If enacted, it would create a comprehensive federal standard that preempts (replaces) many state laws. Until then, businesses must navigate the state-by-state patchwork.</p>

  <div class="warning-box">
    <strong>Practical Advice:</strong> If you handle consumer data in the US, aim for CCPA/CPRA compliance as your baseline. It's the strictest US law, and meeting its requirements will put you in good shape for other states. Or better yet, aim for GDPR compliance — it exceeds all US state laws.
  </div>

  <slot slot="related">
